{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/585938-2e-morbus-reimagening","id":585938,"title":"2e Morbus reimagening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-10T05:57:26-07:00","id":585938,"title":"2e Morbus reimagening","content":"As my first big homebrewing experiment, I decided to on the behalf of one of my players rework the Morbus Bloodline to a 2e mindframe and power level. What I've written below is just mechanics, but do they seem sound? <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Morbus: The Carrion<br /> Parent Clan: Mekhet<br /> Disciplines: Celerity, Obfuscate, Auspex, Cachexy<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Boon</b>: <i>Sense the Taint</i>. The Morbus feed from the diseased, the rotten, the tainted. Centuries of such a specified palate has made them evolve, adapted to a feeding stock of the sick. When invoking their Predatory Senses, the Morbus may also pinpoint any mortal currently carrying some form of transmitted disease. At further Successes, they can also detail what disease it is and what stage of infection the mortal is at. The range of Sense the Taint is limited by Blood Potency, just like any other usage of the Predatory Senses.<br /> <b>Bloodline Weakness:</b> <i>Rotten Taste</i>. The Morbus are carrions of disease by their very nature, to the point where something about the visceral taint is necessary for them to properly develop Vitae. The Morbus can drink blood from any mortal like any other vampire, but clean, untainted blood feels bland, tasteless and without the usual rush of feeding. Worse yet, it does not bestow any power to the Morbus, unable to give even a single point of Vitae no matter the amount of blood taken. To gain Vitae proper, the Morbus must consume blood from the diseased. The disease the mortal carries must be natural, the Cachexy Plague not being sufficient for feeding purposes. If the Morbus feeds from an individual matching this criteria, they gain Vitae like any other Kindred would.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Cachexy</u></b><br /> <b>\u2022 Sickly Touch</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Dexterity + Medicine + Cachexy vs the defender's Stamina<br /> <b>Action:</b> Standard<br /> The Morbus touches a mortal within range who, provided they fail at their reflexive Stamina roll, instantly gain the Cachexy Plague Condition. The mortal cannot spread it to anyone else, but will keep the disease for the Morbus' Blood Potency in weeks.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022 Contaminate</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> None<br /> <b>Roll: </b>Resolve + Medicine + Cachexy<br /> <b>Action:</b> Standard<br /> The Morbus concentrates, either touching the ground or an object, equal or lesser to their level in Cachexy in Size. Upon a successful roll, the Morbus contaminates the chosen object, or an area equal to their Blood Potency in yards (the center being where they touched). If any mortal interacts with the contaminated object or remains on contaminated ground for longer than a minute, they must roll a reflexive Stamina roll. If the roll fails, they instantly gain the Cachexy Plague Condition. The contamination lasts for the successes of the activation roll in days.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022 Intensify Infection</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Intelligence + Medicine + Cachexy<br /> <b>Action:</b> Standard<br /> The Morbus concentrates on an individual with the Cachexy Plague Condition within their line of sight. On a successful roll, the target instantly resolves the Cachexy Plague Condition and instead develops the Deadly Plague Condition. The Deadly Plague Condition remains for as long as the Cachexy Plague Condition had before being resolved.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Pestis Volitantia</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2 Vitae<br /> <b>Roll:</b> Wits + Medicine + Cachexy vs the highest Stamina among the targets<br /> <b>Action:</b> Standard<br /> The Morbus no longer needs to touch their intended victim. Instead, they use their own body more as a vessel for their plague. The Morbus focuses on a group within their line of sight, no more in numbers than the Morbus\u2019 Blood Potency. Upon a successful roll, all the targets gain the Cachexy Plague Condition. Furthermore, the Plague can now be spread from mortal to mortal. If any mortal inflicted with the Cachexy Plague Condition in this manner interacts with another, untainted mortal for longer than five minutes, the healthy mortal has to roll Stamina or gain the Cachexy Plague Condition exactly as if targeted by Cachexy. This newly infected mortal can also spread their disease in the same manner. If the Cachexy Plague Condition is exchanged for the Deadly Plague Condition through Intensify Infection, the mortal still spreads their disease, but victims of this infection gain the Cachexy Plague Condition, not the Deadly Plague Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Plague of the Dead</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Vitae<br /> <b>Roll:</b> None, alters another use of Cachexy<br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> Upon complete mastery of Cachexy, nobody is safe from the Cachexy Plague, not even the Kindred themselves. The Morbus invokes this power before activating another Cachexy ability. For said use, the possible targets are no longer only mortals, but also any vampires within vicinity. Kindred targeted by Cachexy roll Stamina + Blood Potency for resistance, but develop the Cachexy Plague Condition upon a failure just like any mortal. This Condition can also be intensified into the Deadly Plague Condition through the use of Intensify Infection, provided the Morbus also activates Plague of the Dead for that deed.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Conditions</u></b><br /> <b>Cachexy Plague</b><br /> You have been inflicted with the Cachexy Plague, the strange, supernatural disease of the Morbus. There are no bacteria or viruses, yet your body acts as if you are inflicted with a very heavy flu. You get cold sweat, run a high fever, suffer from intense fatigue and gain painful cramps if you remain still for too long. At the beginning of every day you are inflicted with the Cachexy Plague Condition, roll a Stamina roll. On a failed roll, take one Bashing Damage. Furthermore, you have -3 on all Physical Actions. This damage does not heal until the Cachexy Plague Condition is resolved.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The timeframe of infection, the Morbus that inflicted you with the disease's Blood Potency in weeks, runs out. Alternatively, any Morbus with an equal or higher level of Cachexy than the infector can roll Intelligence + Medicine to resolve the Condition ahead of time, provided they get equal or more Successes than the Morbus that infected you\u2019s Cachexy level upon the time of infection.<br /> <br /> <b>Deadly Plague</b><br /> This is something a whole whole lot more than the Cachexy Plague. In addition to the earlier mentioned symptoms, it hurts to breathe, you have shakes and heavy, wet coughs. You are nauseous and will often throw up if given the chance. Furthermore, large boils emerge on your skin, filled with dark blood. Breaking one is extremely painful, and will only prompt more to appear. One would think your body is trying to kill itself, and they would be absolutely right. Instead of Bashing Damage, take one Lethal Damage upon a failed Stamina roll every day. Additionally, infected Kindred lose one point of Vitae every time they take damage this way. You now suffer a -5 on all Physical Actions and a -3 on all other actions. Damage inflicted by the Deadly Plague Condition cannot be healed until the Deadly Plague Condition is resolved.<br /> <b>Beat:</b> n/a<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> The timeframe of the original, now upgraded Cachexy Plague Condition comes to an end. Alternatively, any Morbus with an equal or higher level of Cachexy than the infector can roll Resolve + Medicine to resolve the Condition ahead of time, provided they get equal or more Successes than the Morbus that infected you\u2019s Cachexy level upon the time of infection.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4906,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4906-deraneo","user":"Deraneo","date":". 07-10-2015, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4906-deraneo","name":"Deraneo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:11:10-07:00","id":586230,"title":"","content":"Looks like a fair start to me, although I did have a couple of thoughts:<br /> <br /> 1. Elders can take in weaker, non-Kindred vitae, as long as they spend a point of willpower per point of 'thin' blood. Perhaps having that as an option for their clan weakness might help (i.e. a point of Willpower to ingest non diseased Vitae), without completely obviating it.<br /> <br /> 2. Bloodlines having special disciplines outside the core 10 is supposed to be a fairly rare thing in Blood &amp; Smoke. I was actually thinking about the Morbus in the last couple of days, and wondering if it might be better to have Resilience as their fourth discipline, with Cachexy as either a set of merits or devotions as is usually intended for the new way bloodlines work\u2014for example, by combining Auspex and Resilience in the case of the first level: the former to perceive the subject/target/victim and Resilience as a body discipline to 'project' the illness onto them.<br /> <br /> 3. Regarding the custom conditions for disease from Cachexy, have you considered using conditions like Confused, Drained, or Fatigued for the lower levels?<br /> <br /> 4. Also, how does Cachexy work if projected on Kindred (or other supernaturals)?<br /> <br /> 5. Are the rolls contested or penalized by the target (say, Stamina + Blood Potency)? They currently look to be uncontested or non subtracted at all.<br /> <br /> 6. What about Dramatic Failures and Exceptional Successes on the roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 07-21-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:50:06-07:00","id":586263,"title":"","content":"Here's my latest take on the Morbus for comparison: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1748-blood-and-smoke-bloodline-disciplines-conversions?p=332705#post332705\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...705#post332705</a><br /> <br /> There's some more versions of both Cachexy and the Morbus by PenDragon and me on the Requiem Hombrew Hub thread at the top of the Vampire forums if you like to take a look at other variants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T10:57:51-07:00","id":586267,"title":"","content":"I agree with thinking that Cachexy should be a set of devotions or merits instead of a Discipline. I like the idea that their Bloodline Boon is the ability to sense if a blood is diseased by tasting it and be able to buy Cachexy merits/devotions (it really depends on where you want it placed on the character sheet), including one that allows them to sense diseased humans by smell.<br /> <br /> The Morbus are one of the few Bloodlines I really like, and Resilience fits well with the fact that some diseases are more resilient than others. I'll likely rewrite them for 2e myself, along with the Children of Judas, and was wondering if Deraneo wanted me to split it off into a different thread or was fine with others posting their ideas on this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}